### 3. Additional context (if relevant):                                                                                
- Rationale for inclusion:                                                                                              
  - Study 1 (OPTILOGG): RCT, adults with HF; tablet-based system delivered HF and lifestyle education at home; compared 
with standard information—fits mHealth-delivered education on a mobile device.                                          
  - Study 2 (e-Vita HF): RCT, stable HF; education via heartfailurematters.org website (internet/web-based), compared to
usual care; explicitly educational.                                                                                     
  - Study 4 (SMS vs telephone vs regular): RCT with an SMS arm delivering structured follow-up via text; interpreted as 
SMS-delivered educational/follow-up content; compared to regular/telephone follow-up.                                   
                                                                                                                        
- Key exclusion reasons across the 197 records:                                                                         
  - Not RCTs or not adult HF populations.                                                                               
  - Interventions primarily telemonitoring, remote physiologic monitoring, device follow-up, or counseling/MI/health    
coaching without explicit mHealth-delivered educational content as defined.                                             
  - Web-based programs not clearly designed for mobile/smartphone/tablet use (per protocol focus) or not compared versus
usual HF care.                                                                                                          
  - Study types such as protocols, feasibility/usability, observational studies, reviews/meta-analyses, guidelines,     
policy statements, or non-HF populations.                                                                               
                                                                                                                        
- Uncertainties/assumptions:                                                                                            
  - We applied the protocol’s explicit focus on “mHealth-delivered education” for mobile platforms                      
(smartphones/tablets/other mobile devices) and SMS/social media. Generic desktop-only web education and pure            
telemonitoring without an educational program were excluded.                                                            
  - For study 4, the abstract suggests SMS-based follow-up; we conservatively treated SMS follow-up content as          
educational (consistent with protocol examples), hence INCLUDED. If full text shows purely logistical reminders without 
educational content, it could be excluded at full-text review.                                                          
  - Borderline exclusions (e.g., general web portals not mobile-focused, telemonitoring with automated instructions) can
be re-checked at full-text stage per the conservative include-when-in-doubt principle; however, we prioritized adherence
to the protocol’s mHealth education definition.                                                                         
