  ### 3. Additional context (if relevant):                                                                              
  - Rationale for inclusion:                                                                                            
    - Study 1 (OPTILOGG): RCT, adults with HF; tablet-based system included HF/lifestyle education; compared against    
  standard HF information. Fits mHealth-delivered education on a mobile device.                                         
    - Study 2 (e-Vita HF): RCT, stable HF; education via the ESC/HFA heartfailurematters.org website                    
  (internet/web-based) versus usual care; explicitly educational content.                                               
    - Study 4 (SMS vs telephone vs regular): RCT; SMS arm delivered structured follow-up/educational messaging via      
  text compared to regular/telephone follow-up.                                                                         
                                                                                                                        
  - Common exclusion reasons:                                                                                           
    - Not RCTs; not adult HF populations; wrong comparators.                                                            
    - Telemonitoring/device follow-up or coaching without explicit mHealth-delivered education component as defined in  
  the protocol.                                                                                                         
    - Reviews, protocols, qualitative/usability, observational studies, guidelines/policy; or non-HF or                 
  non-educational interventions.                                                                                        
                                                                                                                        
  - Notes:                                                                                                              
    - Applied the protocol’s narrow definition of “mHealth-delivered education” (smartphone/tablet/other mobile device  
  apps, web-based education for mobile use, SMS, social media) vs usual HF care.                                        
    - Ambiguities (e.g., whether SMS content is strictly educational) can be resolved at full-text stage; we erred on   
  conservative inclusion for study 4 consistent with the protocol’s examples.                                           
  """                                                                                                                   
                                                                                                                        
  final_answer(report)                                                                                                  
