### 2. Task outcome (extremely detailed version):                                                                       
- Protocol applied exactly as written:                                                                                  
  - Population: Adults (≥18) with diagnosed HF.                                                                         
  - Design: Randomized controlled trials.                                                                               
  - Comparator: Usual HF care.                                                                                          
  - Intervention: mHealth-delivered education (internet/web programs used on smartphones/tablets or other mobile        
devices, SMS, social-media delivered education; apps included).                                                         
- Inclusion decisions (IDs 1, 2, 4, 20):                                                                                
  - ID 1: RCT; home tablet + scale system included HF information and lifestyle advice on the tablet. The educational   
content was mHealth-delivered; comparator was standard HF information (usual care). Included.                           
  - ID 2: Three-arm RCT with a website (heartfailurematters.org) intervention versus usual care among stable HF         
outpatients; clear web-based HF education component on top of usual care. Although platform unspecified, typical web    
delivery is mobile-accessible; given conservative stance and direct “website education vs usual care,” Included.        
  - ID 4: Randomized clinical trial comparing SMS follow-up (educational/supportive content conveyed via text) vs       
telephone vs regular follow-up in HF patients; SMS arm fits mHealth education via mobile messaging vs routine care.     
Included.                                                                                                               
  - ID 20: 2:1 randomized trial testing a mobile phone–assisted case management program with self-care education/support
versus usual care among HF patients. Included as mHealth education delivered via mobile phones.                         
- Key exclusions and rationale patterns:                                                                                
  - Not RCTs or non-HF populations or protocols (e.g., feasibility, usability, qualitative, protocols, meta-analyses,   
guidelines): IDs 9, 12–14, 16–19, 29–31, 35–36, 39–41, 42, 44–47, 48–50, 55–57, 60, 62–66, 68–71, 73, 75, 79–81, 83–88, 
90–91, 93–97, 99–107, 109–117, 120–129, 131–132, 134–150, 151, 154–158, 160–162, 164–171, 172–200.                      
  - Telemonitoring/remote monitoring/decision support without a primary educational program comparison vs usual care (or
where education was not clearly mHealth-delivered or not the primary intervention focus): IDs 21–23, 31–34, 37–38, 58,  
67, 71–72, 79–82, 86, 88, 90, 93–95, 120, 124, 137, 140, 147, 149.                                                      
  - In-person or desktop-only education (non-mobile), or hospital video education adjuncts, or general web-based without
clear mHealth/mobile framing (and not explicitly within smartphones/tablets), or wrong comparator: IDs 8, 25–26, 51–54, 
77, 85, 92, 101, 133, 145. Given the protocol’s focus on mHealth modalities, these were excluded.                       
  - Non-educational counseling/MI/psychotherapy telephone programs (behavioral support but not clearly mHealth education
via mobile/web/app/SMS per protocol): IDs 18, 60–61, 84, 141–142, 165.                                                  
  - Device-focused trials (ICDs/CRTs), drug/device economics, and other non-educational interventions: IDs 57, 62–63,   
86, 111, 113, 116, 174.                                                                                                 
  - Borderline considerations handled conservatively in favor of exclusion:                                             
    - ID 3 (pilot RCT of web-based self-care): platform likely desktop; protocol restricts to mHealth delivered         
education on smartphones/tablets/other mobile devices. Absent clear mobile use, Excluded.                               
    - ID 82/166 (mobile phone-based telemonitoring RCTs): included educational instructions but primarily telemonitoring
framework rather than a defined educational program vs usual care. Excluded to adhere strictly to “mHealth-delivered    
education” focus.                                                                                                       
    - ID 77 (patient portal with educational guide): delivery likely desktop/web-based EMR access; primary aim not a    
structured mHealth education program; Excluded.                                                                         
- Conservatism: When unsure whether the educational content was truly mHealth and compared against usual care, I        
excluded to preserve protocol fidelity. Where mobile/web education vs usual care was explicit (IDs 1, 2, 4, 20), I      
included.                                                                                                               
                                                                                                                        
Quality control checks:                                                                                                 
- Exactly 200 unique studies returned (IDs 1–200; deduplicated).                                                        
- Each study object contains only id, title, decision.                                                                  
- Decisions are strictly “INCLUDE” or “EXCLUDE.”                                                                        
- Top-level keys are exactly: title, selection_criteria, studies.                                                       
                                                                                                                        
Counts:                                                                                                                 
- n_total: 200                                                                                                          
- n_included: 4                                                                                                         
- n_excluded: 196                                                                                                       
                                                                                                                        
### 3. Additional context (if relevant):                                                                                
- Potentially eligible but ambiguous studies (e.g., web-based interventions not clearly used on mobile devices, or      
telemonitoring with embedded education) could be revisited at full-text stage. The protocol’s examples highlighted      
smartphone/tablet/app/SMS/social-media delivery; many desktop-only or telemonitoring-heavy trials were therefore        
excluded at this title/abstract stage.                                                                                  
- If the review team decides to broaden “mHealth” to include any internet-based HF education irrespective of device,    
candidates like ID 3 and 77 could be reconsidered.                                                                      
- Sensitivity for inclusion criteria: if telemonitoring trials with structured, protocolized education components and   
clear usual-care comparators are acceptable, some currently excluded RCTs might be revisited.                           
